  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A square shaped hole of side<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> is carved out at a distance&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> from the centre&nbsp;&#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>&#39; of a uniform circular disk of radius a. If the distance of the centre of mass of the remaining portion from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mfrac></math>, value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math> (to the nearest integer) is :</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0071_4181fca87bba.png\" style=\"width: 238px; height: 218px;\" />&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>"
  },
